# Every text file checks out with LF, whatever core.autocrlf says on the machine. The generator
# parses plugin/** from the working tree and compares dist/** byte for byte, so a CRLF checkout
# (core.autocrlf=true on Windows) makes gen:check fail on every .md and leaves "stale" output;
# the hooks read .json and run .sh, which break the same way on Linux and macOS.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Kept explicit: shell scripts and the hook manifest are the files that fail loudest.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf